<title>JAPAN: Seven-Eleven shares hit new 1997 high.</title>
<headline>Seven-Eleven shares hit new 1997 high.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Seven-Eleven Japan Co Ltd rose to a new high for this calendar year on Monday on the belief that the firm's sales are holding firm despite a rise in the nation's consumption tax, brokers said.</p>
<p>The share price of the leading convenience store operator hit 7,920 yen, its highest level so far this year, before easing slightly. At 0405 GMT, it was 50 yen higher at 7,880.</p>
<p>Its trading volume was 145,000 shares.</p>
<p>Japan raised its consumption tax from three to five percent on April 1.</p>
</text>
